@extends('layouts.app')

@section('title')Installation@endsection
@section('description')How to add Orbit to a Rocket.rs app from crates.io, with its derive and blocking features, and the sqlx version a hand-written model needs.@endsection

@section('content')
  <h1>{{ $title }}</h1>
  <p>Orbit is a Rust crate. It needs Rust 1.94.0 or newer, the minimum of its <code>sqlx</code> 0.9.0 dependency (the crate itself uses edition 2024, which needs 1.85), and a server for MySQL, MariaDB, PostgreSQL or SQLite. Orbit is published on <a href="https://crates.io/crates/orbit-orm">crates.io</a> as <code>orbit-orm</code>.</p>

  <h2>Add the crate</h2>
  <pre class="line-numbers"><code class="language-bash">cargo add orbit-orm</code></pre>
  <p>The same dependency in <code>Cargo.toml</code>:</p>
  <pre class="line-numbers"><code class="language-toml">[dependencies]
orbit-orm = "0.1.0"</code></pre>
  <p>The package is <code>orbit-orm</code>, and the Rust crate name is <code>orbit_orm</code>, so the code imports from <code>orbit_orm</code>.</p>

  <h2>Features</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>derive</code>, on by default, adds the <code>OrbitModel</code> derive. See <a href="/docs/models">Models</a>. Without it, write the <code>Model</code> impls by hand.</li>
    <li><code>blocking</code>, off by default, adds <code>orbit_orm::blocking</code>, the synchronous API. See <a href="/docs/blocking">Blocking API</a>.</li>
    <li><code>mysql</code>, on by default, adds MySQL and MariaDB.</li>
    <li><code>postgres</code> adds PostgreSQL, and <code>sqlite</code> adds SQLite. Both are off by default.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>To turn on the blocking API:</p>
  <pre class="line-numbers"><code class="language-bash">cargo add orbit-orm --features blocking</code></pre>
  <p>To add PostgreSQL as well as MySQL:</p>
  <pre class="line-numbers"><code class="language-bash">cargo add orbit-orm --features postgres</code></pre>
  <p>To use SQLite instead of MySQL:</p>
  <pre class="line-numbers"><code class="language-bash">cargo add orbit-orm --no-default-features --features sqlite,derive</code></pre>
  <p>To leave out the derive, turn off the default features and keep <code>mysql</code>:</p>
  <pre class="line-numbers"><code class="language-bash">cargo add orbit-orm --no-default-features --features mysql</code></pre>

  <h2 id="unreleased">Unreleased features</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/docs/schema">schema builder</a> and schema migrations (<code>Migration::schema</code>) are in the main branch of the <a href="https://github.com/lajennylove/Orbit">Orbit repository</a>, not yet on crates.io. <code>orbit-orm</code> 0.1.0 on crates.io does not have them. To use them now, depend on the repository:</p>
  <pre class="line-numbers"><code class="language-toml">[dependencies]
orbit-orm = { git = "https://github.com/lajennylove/Orbit", branch = "main" }</code></pre>
  <p>Switch back to a crates.io version when they are released.</p>

  <h2>Async runtime</h2>
  <p>The async API runs on Tokio. A Rocket app already runs on Tokio, so nothing more is needed. A plain binary needs a runtime, such as <code>#[tokio::main]</code>.</p>

  <h2>Sqlx for hand-written models</h2>
  <p>The derive needs no other crate. A hand-written model implements <code>sqlx</code>'s <code>FromRow</code>, so the app needs <code>sqlx</code> too. Use the version Orbit uses, which is <code>0.9.0</code>, so that both use one copy of it:</p>
  <pre class="line-numbers"><code class="language-toml">sqlx = { version = "0.9.0", default-features = false, features = ["mysql"] }</code></pre>
  <p>See <a href="/docs/models">Models</a> for the hand-written form.</p>
@endsection
